│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ optimize_drone_path_with_gaussian_offsets                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ To minimize the combined score (which is a product of flying distance F1, school noise    │
│                          │ F2, and signal drop F3), we need to modify the drone's path so that it bends away from    │
│                          │ the school to reduce noise (F2) and bends towards the base station to improve signal      │
│                          │ (F3), while keeping the path smooth to avoid excessively increasing the flying distance   │
│                          │ (F1).                                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ We achieve this by:                                                                       │
│                          │ 1. Calculating the baseline straight-line path.                                           │
│                          │ 2. Using Gaussian functions to create smooth local offsets. We push the path away from    │
│                          │ the school's coordinates and pull it towards the base station's coordinates.              │
│                          │ 3. Applying a sine window function to the offsets so that the path smoothly connects to   │
│                          │ the exact start and end points without any abrupt jumps, which would otherwise heavily    │
│                          │ penalize the distance score (F1).                                                         │
