│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ active_contours_path                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ This approach uses a physics-based "Active Contours" (Snakes) algorithm. Instead of a     │
│                          │ straight line or simple geometric heuristic, it models the drone path as a flexible       │
│                          │ string. We define an energy function with three components: internal smoothness (to       │
│                          │ minimize flying distance), repulsion from the school (to minimize noise), and attraction  │
│                          │ to the base station (to minimize signal drop). By applying gradient descent, the path     │
│                          │ iteratively deforms to find the optimal balance between these three competing objectives, │
│                          │ naturally bending away from the school and towards the base station.                      │
