│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ surrogate_multiobjective_grid_search                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The previous implementation used a strictly straight flight path, yielding a high MOP     │
│                          │ multiplier score because it ignored school noise and signal drop.                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ As instructed, we need to create a smooth line that selectively bends away from the       │
│                          │ school located near (40, 20) to minimize noise impact (F2), and bends towards the base    │
│                          │ station near (70, -30) to minimize signal drop (F3), while paying a small tension penalty │
│                          │ on travel distance (F1).                                                                  │
│                          │ Since the overall MOP Multiplier score is heavily dependent on the product of F1, F2, and │
│                          │ F3 (based on empirical scores from straight lines F1: 1.000, F2: 2.227, F3: 43.199, MOP:  │
│                          │ 96.228 ≈ F1×F2×F3), we can design a proxy/surrogate score function right inside our       │
│                          │ method and then use a zero-dependency deterministic grid-search to find the absolute      │
│                          │ optimal amount of gaussian deflection for the line!                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key implementations:                                                                      │
│                          │ 1. Define parametric Gaussian deformations added to the straight line that pushes away    │
│                          │ from the school and towards the base station.                                             │
│                          │ 2. Formulate a fully analytical and monotonic proxy approximation internal to the         │
│                          │ function to simulate the F1, F2 F3 tradeoffs on-the-fly.                                  │
│                          │ 3. Rapidly grid search across deformation amplitudes (`A_school`, `A_base`) and width     │
│                          │ (`W_choices`) to identify the minimum internal MOP score and deploy exactly that smoothly │
│                          │ bent coordinate series.                                                                   │
│                          │ 4. Uses fused calculations arrayed dynamically, allowing ~350,000 internal simulated      │
│                          │ evaluations smoothly within milliseconds entirely inside `evolve_drone_path`.             │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0513                                                                                   │
