│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ smooth_gaussian_potential_field                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ The algorithm replaces the naive linear interpolation with a Gaussian-modulated potential │
│                          │ field. Traditional pathfinding often uses piecewise heuristics which increase the F1      │
│                          │ (Distance) penalty and lack smoothness.                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Instead, I model the drone path as a baseline linear trajectory modified by an            │
│                          │ "attractor" force.                                                                        │
│                          │ 1. **Targeting Objectives**: Since the path needs to avoid the school (40, 20) and        │
│                          │ approach the base station (70, -30), both objectives are satisfied by a smooth deflection │
│                          │ in the negative Y-direction.                                                              │
│                          │ 2. **Smoothness (F1)**: By using a Gaussian kernel centered near x=65, we ensure the      │
│                          │ deflection is infinitely differentiable, minimizing the "extra distance" penalty while    │
│                          │ maximizing the avoidance/proximity gains.                                                 │
│                          │ 3. **Boundary Constraints**: To maintain the start and end connection, the deflection is  │
│                          │ multiplied by a parabolic envelope $4 \cdot t \cdot (1-t)$, which pins the displacement   │
│                          │ to zero at the endpoints.                                                                 │
│                          │ 4. **Weights**: The amplitude and sigma are tuned to prioritize the F3 (Signal Loss)      │
│                          │ reduction, as it is the most dominant penalty in the current evaluation.                  │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
