│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ adam_physics_path_optimizer                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ To minimize the combined score (which is the product of F1, F2, and F3), we can           │
│                          │ mathematically reframe the problem as minimizing the sum of their logarithms: `log(F1) +  │
│                          │ log(F2) + log(F3)`.                                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ We can model this using a physics-inspired gradient descent approach:                     │
│                          │ 1. **F1 (Flying Distance)** acts as a tension force, pulling the path into a straight     │
│                          │ line.                                                                                     │
│                          │ 2. **F2 (School Noise Proximity)** acts as a repulsive force, pushing the path away from  │
│                          │ the school.                                                                               │
│                          │ 3. **F3 (Base Station Signal Drop)** acts as an attractive force, pulling the path        │
│                          │ towards the base station.                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ By computing the relative gradients (`grad(F) / F`) for each objective at every point, we │
│                          │ perfectly balance these three conflicting forces without needing to guess their exact     │
│                          │ weighting constants. We implement a lightweight Adam Optimizer from scratch in pure       │
│                          │ Python to iteratively adjust the Y-coordinates. Adam normalizes the gradients, preventing │
│                          │ numerical instability if the drone gets too close to the school, and ensures smooth       │
│                          │ convergence within the 12-second timeout.                                                 │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
