│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ heuristic_parameter_tuning_and_envelope_optimization                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current heuristic path optimization is limited by three factors:                      │
│                          │ 1) The clipping of the path offset (max_offset=22.0) prevents the drone from reaching the │
│                          │ base station's Y-coordinate (approx -30), leading to high signal loss (F3).               │
│                          │ 2) The school repulsion and base attraction weights are too conservative.                 │
│                          │ 3) The sinusoidal envelope is too narrow at the points of interest (x=40 and x=70).       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit improves the path by:                                                           │
│                          │ - Increasing the max_offset to 60.0 to allow full proximity to the base station.          │
│                          │ - Using a power-transformed sine envelope (sin^0.7) to create a flatter "plateau" in the  │
│                          │ middle of the path, allowing the drone to stay near the base station for a longer         │
│                          │ duration.                                                                                 │
│                          │ - Implementing dynamic repulsion that scales with the distance between the baseline and   │
│                          │ the school, ensuring a more consistent clearance.                                         │
│                          │ - Increasing the influence (sigma) of both the school and base station to create          │
│                          │ smoother, earlier transitions that minimize the product of F1, F2, and F3.                │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
