│ patch_name               │ active_contour_adam                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ This structural redesign radically shifts from stochastic search (Cross-Entropy Method)   │
│                          │ over fixed basis functions to a pointwise Active Contour approach directly driven by the  │
│                          │ Adam optimizer. Because the ultimate ranking metric is the multiplicative product `F1 *   │
│                          │ F2 * F3`, the program precisely optimizes `log(F1) + log(F2) + log(F3)`. The natural log  │
│                          │ automatically balances the magnitudes of the raw objective gradients, allowing forces     │
│                          │ representing path elasticity, school repulsion, and base attraction to harmonize          │
│                          │ perfectly without arbitrary scaling magic.                                                │
│                          │ It evaluates several initial paths (straight line, heuristically bent curves),            │
│                          │ iteratively runs the Adam optimizer on their individual coordinates through fully         │
│                          │ analytical gradients, applies a discrete high-order Laplacian penalty for rigid curvature │
│                          │ preservation, and then yields the path offering the minimized combined log loss. This     │
│                          │ results in incredibly smooth, dynamically adapting curves that aggressively plunge the    │
│                          │ combined Multi-Objective score.                                                           │
