│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ annealed_gauss_seidel_band                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Transitions the optimization scheme to a Direct Successive Over-Relaxation (SOR)          │
│                          │ Pointwise Solver (Gauss-Seidel). Rather than computing relative gradients for an Adam     │
│                          │ optimizer, this approach treats the path as an elastic band being acted upon directly by  │
│                          │ repulsion and attraction field forces. I implemented a 3000-sweep scheduler that smoothly │
│                          │ shifts from a "carving phase" (high beta: school repulsion) to a "fine-tuning phase"      │
│                          │ (high gamma: base attraction). This elegantly leverages Gauss-Seidel stability to achieve │
│                          │ smooth global deflections without exploding learning gradients, directly addressing the   │
│                          │ recommendation to minimize F3 without sacrificing the F2 clearance.                       │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0435                                                                                   │
