│ patch_description        │ I propose replacing the single-scale 12-control coordinate descent with a hierarchical    │
│                          │ coarse-to-fine optimization over the same Gaussian control family.                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Why this should help:                                                                     │
│                          │ 1. **Better global geometry first**: a small control model (5 controls) explores          │
│                          │ large-shape bending more reliably, reducing risk of early local minima.                   │
│                          │ 2. **Then refine details**: interpolate the coarse solution into 12 controls and continue │
│                          │ local optimization for fine adjustments.                                                  │
│                          │ 3. **Directional priors aligned with objectives**: initialization explicitly bends away   │
│                          │ from school and toward base using line-relative direction signs, which matches the        │
│                          │ requested behavior and usually improves F2/F3 tradeoff.                                   │
│                          │ 4. **Still objective-aligned**: score remains the exact proxy product `F1 * F2 * F3`, so  │
│                          │ improvements directly target evaluator behavior.                                          │
│                          │ 5. **Smoothness maintained**: same Gaussian basis plus a tiny final smoothing pass keeps  │
│                          │ path realistic and prevents noisy overfitting.                                            │
