│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ asymmetric_local_seeds                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ This edit strengthens the current optimizer without rewriting the whole function.         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The main idea is to keep the existing Gaussian-control representation, but make it much   │
│                          │ more search-efficient for the actual objective:                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Add a smooth endpoint envelope to the Gaussian deformation basis, so bends naturally   │
│                          │ taper to zero near start/end. This usually reduces unnecessary path length inflation      │
│                          │ while preserving the ability to bend strongly near important regions.                     │
│                          │ 2. Precompute basis values and score constants, making it cheap to evaluate many more     │
│                          │ candidate paths.                                                                          │
│                          │ 3. Replace the symmetric school/base initialization sweep with a richer seed set that is  │
│                          │ explicitly asymmetric and event-localized:                                                │
│                          │    - single bump before the school,                                                       │
│                          │    - single bump after the school,                                                        │
│                          │    - left-heavy school repulsion,                                                         │
│                          │    - right-heavy school repulsion,                                                        │
│                          │    - a bridge bump between school and base,                                               │
│                          │    - directional seeds that bend away from the school and toward the base.                │
│                          │ 4. Instead of optimizing only one best seed, rank all seeds and run coordinate descent    │
│                          │ from the top few. This increases basin coverage and is especially useful in this          │
│                          │ landscape where localized bends around the school and base matter more than globally      │
│                          │ symmetric perturbations.                                                                  │
│                          │ 5. Add a final light smoothing pass to preserve a smooth line shape while keeping the     │
│                          │ beneficial bend away from (40, 20) and toward (70, -30).                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This is directly aimed at reducing the product F1 * F2 * F3 by improving initialization   │
│                          │ quality and preserving smoothness with lower distance overhead.                           │
