│ patch_description        │ This structural redesign introduces an adaptive control-point architecture. Instead of    │
│                          │ optimizing dense Y-coordinates directly or using fixed RBF centers, the path is           │
│                          │ parameterized by a set of movable control points `(cx, cy)`. Both the Y-coordinates and   │
│                          │ X-coordinates of these control points are optimized simultaneously using Adam. By         │
│                          │ allowing the X-coordinates to shift, the model dynamically reallocates representational   │
│                          │ capacity to regions that need it most (e.g., sharp bends near the school or base). Exact  │
│                          │ analytical gradients are backpropagated through linear interpolation to update the        │
│                          │ control points, and a Laplacian spring force ensures the X-coordinates maintain monotonic │
│                          │ ordering and avoid collapsing.                                                            │
