│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ analytic_multistart_adam                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ This approach transitions from discrete point-based evaluation approximations to exact    │
│                          │ continuous curve line integrals utilizing a 3-point Gaussian Quadrature scheme. This      │
│                          │ computes precise path lengths (F1), school proximity repulsions (F2), and base signal     │
│                          │ attritions (F3) natively along each segment, perfectly simulating the evaluator.          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Because the system inherently minimizes the multiplied combined objective MOP = F1 * F2 * │
│                          │ F3, computing explicit analytic integrated gradients for `log(F1) + log(F2) + log(F3)`    │
│                          │ ensures an optimal update direction unaffected by the huge numerical scaling              │
│                          │ discrepancies among the three metrics.                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ To overcome potential saddle points or local topological minima (e.g. passing             │
│                          │ symmetrically above or below the school), it relies on a multi-start strategy. Four       │
│                          │ separate initial trajectory shapes (straight line, mathematically bowing upwards,         │
│                          │ mathematically bowing downwards, and initially biased towards the target base station)    │
│                          │ are optimized with an annealed Adam optimizer for 1500 local steps each. The outcome with │
│                          │ the mathematically lowest final integrated objective cost is definitively selected and    │
│                          │ returned.                                                                                 │
