│ patch_description        │ We introduce `YSFineTuner`, an entirely new secondary local search phase that operates    │
│                          │ directly on the discrete `y` coordinates rather than global macroscopic curve parameters. │
│                          │ While the initial parametric search finds an excellent global structure (avoiding major   │
│                          │ local minima), single-point adjustments are strictly limited. By testing joint sequential │
│                          │ updates on adjacent pairs and triples `(e.g., y)` with combinations from `{-h, 0, h}`,    │
│                          │ the new fine-tuner discovers coordinated block moves. These easily create localized       │
│                          │ shapes that curve efficiently around the school or bend towards the base.                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ To ensure safety and performance, the block search acts as a localized steepest-ascent    │
│                          │ hill climber—evaluating all base deltas, capturing the single most promising              │
│                          │ score-improving configuration before locking it in and continuing the sweep. Alongside    │
│                          │ this, `SurrogateEvaluator.score` was fully optimized to operate with direct index mapping │
│                          │ rather than building temporary `pts` list arrays matching bounds, yielding much faster    │
